{"ticker":"NOCIL","symbol":"NOCIL","instrumentId":3023073,"name":"Nocil","industry":"NSE-Chemicals-Specialty","about":"NOCIL Ltd. is a leading Indian company specializing in the manufacturing of rubber chemicals used in tire and non-tire rubber applications. The company’s product portfolio includes accelerators, antioxidants, pre-vulcanization inhibitors, and other specialty chemicals that improve the performance, longevity, and quality of rubber products. NOCIL operates state-of-the-art manufacturing facilities with a strong emphasis on sustainability, research, and innovation. It caters to a diverse clientele, including global tire manufacturers, footwear, automotive, and industrial rubber goods sectors. With a robust distribution network and commitment to quality, NOCIL has established itself as a reliable supplier in the international rubber chemicals market.","website":"www.nocil.com","location":"Mumbai, INDIA","exchange":"NSE","fetchedAt":"2026-11-20T13:45:23.018Z","basis":"consolidated","price":{"value":138.77,"changePct":1.536547889075893,"week52High":206.3,"week52Low":128.23},"stats":[{"label":"Market capitalization","value":"₹2,318 Cr"},{"label":"Sales","value":"₹1,476 Cr"},{"label":"Shares in float","value":"110,248,000"},{"label":"No. of funds","value":"103"},{"label":"Shares held by funds","value":"20,454,177"},{"label":"Dividend yield","value":"1.08%"},{"label":"Book value","value":"1.31"},{"label":"U/D vol ratio","value":"1.4"},{"label":"LTDebt / equity","value":"—"},{"label":"Alpha","value":"-0.04"},{"label":"Beta","value":"0.86"},{"label":"EPS growth rate","value":"-19%"},{"label":"P/E ratio","value":"29.72"},{"label":"5-year P/E range","value":"22–53"},{"label":"Return on equity","value":"3.1%"},{"label":"Cash flow (INR)","value":"15.09"},{"label":"Volume","value":"197,549"},{"label":"Avg volume (50d)","value":"1,352,632"},{"label":"Master score","value":"53"},{"label":"EPS rating","value":"42"},{"label":"Price strength","value":"33"},{"label":"Gro